ning of day two i'm working  on the billet game plan is to split it  and start forging out the tang i've  noticed that there's a couple cracks i'm  going to grind down through those areas  and see if they've grinded out as i get  closer to my final shape my plan for  getting the tang to attach i'm going to  cut a little notch to the length of my  tang so then we'll heat it up chisel  down push that out and dried our tang  finish our blade now it's just drawing  it out to length to make sure i meet  parameters  going into the quench i'm feeling a  little nervous  those cracks in the blade that i'd seen  earlier i think i've got them ground  down  i think we dodged a bullet on this one i  think it's looking really good  so i start today off with a problem with  my tang my tang is just way too skinny  as well as short i cut two pieces of  high carbon steel fit them up next to my  tang i weld them to make it wider and  longer  but with so much going right eventually  something's going to go wrong  my breaker blew i'll be back in one  second  i really hope this isn't a reoccurring  issue today i have a lot of work to do  when i build my quench tank and there's  a lot of welding involved to do so  my quench tank is gonna be like a trough  style i'm gonna horizontally quench it  so i'm getting ready to weld and i'm  thinking it's gonna be fine as soon as  it tries to start poof my breaker goes  out  so back and forth and back and forth so  many many trips to the breaker later i  have a finished quench tank i feel good  now i'm happy what a pain in the ass  that was man  now i've got to get it quenched  so i go into the oil and i've got this  thing quenched straight skates like  glass solid is an oak i couldn't be  happier  top of day four the game plan for today  is put the final edge on the blade and  then try to get the wood section of this  build figured out i've got a section of  osage orange that i've been working on  and i've got another section of african  ebony i'd